# FPS-MAC-2: the editor an agent's scenario plays on Mac. play_scenario.py and scripts/Dev/_common.sh build and run the
# host's row of scripts/Dev/dev_config.txt (Darwin = Release, the UE Development build) instead of a hard-coded -O0 Debug.
# Before = the Debug editor of the same commit, after = Release; the same view, the per-pass table (profile-dump in
# editor.log: cpu/gpu ms per scope) after each block of frames. The picture must not change.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce --gpu-profile
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда frames 60
Когда profile-dump
Тогда fpsmac2_still WP_Protocol from the scene camera: landscape, town, bushes, sky drawn; frame time in the stat line
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Glide -10
Когда frames 60
Когда profile-dump
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Glide 0
Когда frames 10
Тогда fpsmac2_fly the view 6 m farther along the camera: the same landscape, town and sky, nothing missing or black
